  "2026 Q9": {"marks":7,"subject":"A tree diagram of two delays, expected costs, and a choice of control measures.","rows":[{"for":"complete tree diagram","shows":"see note 1","part":"(a)(i)"},{"for":"calculate combined probabilities","shows":"see note 1","part":"(a)(i)"},{"for":"calculate the probability of a delay occurring","shows":"\\(0.3625\\)","part":"(a)(ii)"},{"for":"calculate the expected cost of a delay","shows":"(£)\\(43{,}500\\)","part":"(a)(iii)"},{"for":"calculate expected cost using control measure 1","shows":"(£)\\(38{,}000\\)","part":"(b)(i)"},{"for":"calculate expected cost using control measure 2","shows":"(£)\\(42{,}500\\)","part":"(b)(ii)"},{"for":"give valid explanation","shows":"using both control measures has the lowest **expected** cost OR (£)\\(32{,}500\\) is the lowest **expected** cost","part":"(c)"}],"notes":["(a) 1. (i) Completed tree: manufacturing delay \\(0.25\\), no manufacturing delay \\(0.75\\); then delivery delay \\(0.15\\), no delivery delay \\(0.85\\) on each branch. Combined: delay, delay \\(0.0375\\); delay, no delay \\(0.2125\\); no delay, delay \\(0.1125\\); no delay, no delay \\(0.6375\\).","(a) 2. (i) Accept fraction and percentage equivalents.","(a) 3. (i) Do not accept any rounding.","(a) 4. (ii) •³ is not available for a probability greater than 1.","(a) 5. (ii) Accept fraction and percentage equivalent.","(a) 6. (iii) •⁴ is still available for using a probability greater than 1 in (a)(ii).","(b) 1. •⁶ is only available where the calculation in •⁵ includes the penalty (£120,000) or the expected cost of the delay calculated in (a)(iii).","(c) 1. Answer must be consistent with (b)(i) and (b)(ii).","(c) 2. Accept: a. 'they' have the lowest **expected** cost; b. it has the lowest **expected** cost.","(c) 3. Do not accept: a. 'cheaper'; b. the cost is less.","(c) 4. •⁷ is not available where •⁵ or •⁶ have not been attempted."]},
  "2026 Q10": {"marks":5,"subject":"A present value, a comparison with inflation, and an insurance excess.","rows":[{"for":"identify multiplier within context","shows":"eg \\(\\text{PV} \\times 1.071^3 = 8175\\) stated or implied by •²","part":"(a)"},{"for":"calculate minimum deposit","shows":"(£)\\(6654.57\\)","part":"(a)"},{"for":"interpret change from CPI","shows":"eg \\(\\dfrac{133.0}{111.4}\\)","part":"(b)"},{"for":"interpret relative increase in savings and state conclusion","shows":"\\(1.228\\ldots\\) and \\(1.193\\ldots\\) leading to 'yes'","part":"(b)"},{"for":"valid reason","shows":"eg protect no claims bonus OR eg so that future premiums are not affected","part":"(c)"}],"notes":["(a) 1. Accept (£)6654.56.","(b) 1. Calculations must be consistent with answer from (a).","(b) 2. For •³, accept any appropriate CPI ratio which can be interpreted from \\(\\dfrac{133.0}{111.4}\\) and \\(\\dfrac{8175}{6654.57}\\).","(c) 1. Accept: a. cost isn't too much more; b. can't afford the excess; c. not worth the effort of claiming to save £15; d. so that cost at renewal is not affected.","(c) 2. Do not accept: a. so that future payments do not increase; b. don't get it repaired; c. cost of insurance will increase."]},
  "2026 Q11": {"marks":5,"subject":"Questioning a data source and a headline, then an estimate from assumptions.","rows":[{"for":"appropriate comment","shows":"eg some beekeepers might not take part so the data might not be accurate OR eg data is self-submitted so there could be errors in the numbers entered","part":"(a)"},{"for":"appropriate explanation","shows":"eg newspaper statement based on extrapolation; future cannot be predicted from data provided OR the trend line does not take into account all the data points","part":"(b)"},{"for":"state assumption for number of honeybees per colony","shows":"eg \\(10\\,000\\) – \\(100\\,000\\) bees","part":"(c)"},{"for":"state assumption for weight of honey in one jar","shows":"eg 100 grams – 1 kilogram","part":"(c)"},{"for":"calculate estimate","shows":"eg \\(288311 \\times \\dfrac{\\text{number of bees}}{17000} \\times\\) number of months \\(\\times\\) weight of honey in one jar \\(=\\) estimated weight of honey","part":"(c)"}],"notes":["(a) 1. Accept: does not include beehives in the wild.","(a) 2. Do not accept: a. honeybees have died; b. some hives have been destroyed after the count.","(b) 1. Accept: the graph has no pattern to it.","(b) 2. Do not accept: bees will reproduce.","(c) 1. •³ and •⁴ can be awarded for reasonable estimates outwith the examples in the illustrative scheme.","(c) 2. If •³ or •⁴ are not attempted then •⁵ is not available.","(c) 3. •⁵ is available for candidates who use 12 months in their calculation without an explicit assumption.","(c) 4. Do not penalise candidates for stating valid, additional assumptions and using them in their calculations."]},
